[[2047,32,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The supply to the speedometer module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               reaches\npin 9 of connector A directly from the battery (maxifuse J/B1of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              )\nvia fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; the supply controlled\nby the ignition (INT) reaches pin 10 of connector A from the line\nprotected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pin 1 of connector A is earthed.</p><p>The ABS control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends the\nspeedometer signal to pin 11 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The speedometer signal is sent again from\npin 15 of connector A to the climate control system control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              andfrom\npin 16 of connector A towards the engine management control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"],[2047,32,2,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The same signal is sent from pin 14 of connector\nA to the automatic transmission control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M54</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"],[2047,32,64,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The same signal is sent from pin 14 of connector\nA to the electronics of the headlamp\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F10A</strong></p>"],[2047,32,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The ABS control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               also sends\nthe &#x27;ABS failure&#x27; signal to pin 6 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              which\nlights up the warning light.</p><p>The signals for the handbrake switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nbrake fluid level sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K25</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               both reach pin 7 of connector\nA of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>The low brake fluid level and\nhandbrake warning light also comes on upon a command from the ABS\ncontrol unit., together with the ABS failure warning light, to indicate\na fault in the EBD braking system.</p></aside><p>If it comes on by itself, the brake fluid\nlevel is low or the handbrake is on.</p><p>The earth signals which provide information\non the state of wear of the brake pads, coming from sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K20,</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              reach\npin 11 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The zeroing signal for the trip meter reaches\npin 12 of connector B from \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; an earth signal from \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               reaches\npin 6 of connector B; according to the logic processed by the internal\nelectronic device, the speedometer receives the side lights on signal\nat pin 5 of connector B and sends the lighting signal to the other\ninstruments: to the centre instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from pin 12 of\nconnector A; and to the rev counter \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from pin 4 of connector\nB \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3233955\">E2530</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>A signal reaches pin 3 of connector B from\nthe left front door switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which signals that the door\nis open.</p><p>Pin 2 of connectorA of\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              receives\nthe earth signal from the switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>l45</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , located on the driver&#x27;s\nseat anchorage, which indicates that the belt is fastened: this\nsignal is sent again from pin 3 of connector A to the check module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234338\">E4022</a></p><p>Pin 8 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\nthe engine rpm signal from the rev counter \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>A serial line connects module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               -\nfrom pin 8 of connector A - to the Infocenter module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E63</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pins 2 and 7 of connector B receive (positive\nand negative) signals coming from the fuel gauge \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               located\nin the fuel pump assembly: these signals are then sent again - from\npins 9 and 10 of connector B - to the centre instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong><a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"],[704,32,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The information concerning the engine oil\nlevel arrives from sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K32 at pins 5 and 13 of connector A\nof E10 and is sent again from pin 8  to connector A of module E63\nwhich displays it.</strong></p>"],[2047,32,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>For all the other warning lights, refer\nto the diagrams for the components to which they refer.</p>"]]